# README - Bucket Sort

## Aim
This folder demonstrates sorting integers with bucket sort using both arrays and linked lists.

---

## Algorithm
1. Find the minimum and maximum input values.
2. Distribute values into buckets based on their offset within that range.
3. Sort values within each bucket.
4. Visit buckets in order and collect their values into the sorted result.

---

## How it works
`Bucket_Sort_array.cpp` creates a bucket for each integer value in the input range, then sorts each bucket before copying the values back. `Bucket_Sort_Linked_list.cpp` distributes existing list nodes among a number of buckets based on their values, inserts nodes into each bucket in sorted order, and concatenates the buckets. Both implementations support negative integers.

---

## Functionality
- Sort integer data in ascending order
- Demonstrate bucket storage using vectors or linked lists

---

## Time and Space Complexity
- Array version: O(n + k) time, plus the cost of sorting within buckets; O(k + n) extra space, where k is the integer range
- Linked-list version: O(n^2) worst-case time because sorted insertion into a bucket may scan its nodes; O(n) bucket references and no additional data nodes
